            <div xml:id="d143">

                <pb facs="0272" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg178"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.348 Z 4/162: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-09-17T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 17,
                                1924—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received September 17—2:12
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>407. Your [<hi rendition="#italic">My</hi>] 404, September 13, 1 p.m.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d143-f1"/> Permission granted but French authorities request
                    that certain fortified seaports be avoided and suppose Zeppelin will have
                    American officers on board and will fly the American flag.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
